oom, upgrade-witness, each with the archive wake of any lending room. The rate read after the window should name the new room's objects, so later baselines separate them from the old rooms.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The route uses the installed-register list as designed and needs no code.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The pins widen only which definitions a planned install may use. The current root still controls every parentless creation.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\n## Ordering condition for the planner\n\nUntil head Q lands, any `deploy.mjs lending` from the tracked file reverts dap-lending to the single old root and strands upgrade-witness. The note says so. U4-B's conditions (2afeefb3) list UC-P, the window, the checks, the `SCREEN_HOSTS` head and U4-T, but not Q. The `SCREEN_HOSTS` head and U4-T each change `wrangler.lending.jsonc` and each ends in a lending deployment. So Q must land before either is deployed, or each must be built on Q. I will check this on each of those heads.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing and runs the window.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1bb24897f1d0b706450df3737ace450236cfcaf2","binding":"assigned","head":"2073ca89d8cfaeda333936daf4b1d4ee7db10d46","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:89967ff88bcdbb9b0cc1b0b7cf83f21446c88da1\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02e2baf9c47624ff4e4a8e627cdd51a071a4ef1e\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:89967ff88bcdbb9b0cc1b0b7cf83f21446c88da1","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}